A||||7||Uaana||Grand Am wheels?||||5||
Z||000000||Uaana||04-30-2000||05:01 AM||||I noticed the post about bonni wheels and why they won't fit. but will the wheels off of a newer grand am GT fit? I like the looks of the three blade plus it has the pontiac stamp on one blade to keep it in the family I'm pretty sure they are 16's but don't know about the bolt pattern.||||reg||5
Z||000001||phillip||04-30-2000||06:44 AM||||i get grand am's and grand prix's mixed up sometimes. if the  grand am is the smaller of the two i think they will fit.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||04-30-2000||08:25 AM||||The grand Prix uses the larger size bolt pattern. The Grand Am wheels are the some bolt pattern as the Fiero. The only thing you might have to look out for is the off-set.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FUEGO V8||04-30-2000||12:08 PM||||I know that 87-91 Beretta and 87-90 Grand Am will fit, including rear rotor and caliper swap. Front swap will need some mods but if you're keeping stock brakes then wheels will fit fine. This might be a cheaper alternative if you like these wheels.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||04-30-2000||02:08 PM||||Hey Fuego V8, welcome. I "met" Fuego V8 over on the 67-72 Chevy/GMC truck forum and found out he is a Fiero guy too, so I invited him over here to check out our Fiero Forum. Yep, must of us know about the Grand Am brake swap and several of us have done it, including me. Lots of old topics about it. This is the best Fiero site on the web, I think you'll agree.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierosound||04-30-2000||06:44 PM||||More websites on wheels.  OEM is what you want to "keep it in the family".<P><BR>Fits Fiero  - <A HREF="http://fiero2m4.homestead.com/Wheels.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fiero2m4.homestead.com/Wheels.html</A> <P>OEM Wheels - <A HREF="http://ackerwheel.com/inven.html" TARGET=_blank>http://ackerwheel.com/inven.html</A> <P>Wheels - <A HREF="http://autopedia.com/html/Wheel.html" TARGET=_blank>http://autopedia.com/html/Wheel.html</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000006||RobertVol||04-30-2000||10:15 PM||||Here is something else that you check out///its kinda of neat.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Downs/9259/2m4.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Downs/9259/2m4.htm</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||05-01-2000||09:08 AM||||FUEGO V8 (and all others)--The BBS style wheels from a '90 Beretta GT will not fit with the stock suspension.  I tried some from my brother-in-laws car.  They bolt up just fine, but the back spacing is wrong.  Maybe with coilovers...||||reg||1
